speechtext:
I want the hon. member to withdraw something he has just said also. The records of this house will show that when the Minister of Labour was putting through his estimates I stated the position very clearly;
I told him of the cheque I had received from the department, diagonally across which was written the words "Relief No. 1." I directed a question to the minister in that regard, but he had no information. Now I want the hon. member for Regina to withdraw the allegation or the insinuation that I received that money from some source other than the source from which I said I received it. That is the point.

Redistribution-Mr. Turnbull
